project LLMRECOG_PHASE_2_PARSE_VALIDATE_SHOW:
  version 6
  title "llmrecog Phase 2 dogfood-first parse, validate, and show slice"
  description |
    Refine only the Phase 2 read path into fixture-first, test-backed vertical slices against semantic contract 0.1, with an evidence review and replan gate after each usable slice.
    Relative complexity points are estimated independently from elapsed time; no velocity, calendar forecast, or delivery date is declared before measured work exists.
    Phase 2 dogfooding means reading repository specifications, authoring bounded .recog documents, and exercising deterministic validate/show behavior; it does not mean provider-generated recognition.
    This plan does not authorize Phase 3 CSP behavior, source locator verification, provider integration, release, publication, or related-repository changes.
  duration_unit point
  finish PHASE_2_ACCEPTED

resource IMPLEMENTER:
  title "Phase 2 implementation capacity"
  capacity 1

resource SEMANTIC_REVIEWER:
  title "Contract and semantic-boundary review capacity"
  description "Only one public-contract or acceptance review runs at a time"
  capacity 1

milestone EXECUTABLE_CONTRACT_0_1_ACCEPTED:
  title "Executable text and result contract 0.1 accepted"
  state reached

milestone PHASE_2_CONTRACT_ACCEPTED:
  title "Phase 2 public result and fixture contract accepted"

milestone DOGFOOD_PROTOCOL_ACCEPTED:
  title "Phase 2 dogfood corpus, questions, receipts, and feedback gates accepted"

milestone BOOTSTRAP_READ_PATH_ACCEPTED:
  title "Minimal source, span, entity, and record read path accepted for private self-use"

milestone GRAMMAR_DOGFOOD_OBSERVED:
  title "Grammar-first authoring dogfood evidence captured"

milestone GRAMMAR_DOGFOOD_REVIEWED:
  title "Grammar-first dogfood feedback dispositioned and plan updated"

milestone COMPLETE_READ_PATH_ACCEPTED:
  title "Complete 0.1 parse, reference, validation, and read-only command path accepted"

milestone SPEC_DOGFOOD_OBSERVED:
  title "Cross-specification authoring dogfood evidence captured"

milestone SPEC_DOGFOOD_REVIEWED:
  title "Cross-specification dogfood feedback dispositioned and plan updated"

milestone PHASE_2_ACCEPTED:
  title "Phase 2 parse, validate, and show vertical slice accepted"

task FREEZE_PHASE_2_CONTRACT EXECUTABLE_CONTRACT_0_1_ACCEPTED -> PHASE_2_CONTRACT_ACCEPTED:
  title "Freeze and accept the Phase 2 public contract"
  description |
    Record the public command and result decision in an accepted ADR before implementation. Add schemas and text/JSON expectations for document show and recognition show, one AST round-trip golden, and exact diagnostic span/code goldens for every Phase 1 invalid fixture. Freeze objective, acceptance, Non-goals, semantic version 0.1, command routes, exit behavior, ordering, completeness, and truncation while keeping implementation and later phases separately gated.
  duration 8p
  status done
  priority 100
  requires:
    IMPLEMENTER 1
    SEMANTIC_REVIEWER 1

task FREEZE_DOGFOOD_PROTOCOL PHASE_2_CONTRACT_ACCEPTED -> DOGFOOD_PROTOCOL_ACCEPTED:
  title "Freeze the Phase 2 dogfood protocol and bounded corpus"
  description |
    Freeze docs/grammar.md and contracts/llmrecog-0.1.ebnf as the first corpus, followed by requirements, terminology, architecture, and implementation phases. Define explicit understanding questions, manually authored .recog inputs, reproducible command receipts, evidence categories, and accepted/rejected/deferred feedback disposition. Dogfood artifacts remain evidence and do not become normative fixtures without separate review.
  duration 5p
  status done
  priority 90
  requires:
    IMPLEMENTER 1
    SEMANTIC_REVIEWER 1

task IMPLEMENT_BOOTSTRAP_READ_PATH DOGFOOD_PROTOCOL_ACCEPTED -> BOOTSTRAP_READ_PATH_ACCEPTED:
  title "Implement the smallest privately usable read path"
  description |
    Add success and failure fixtures, then implement the real bytes-to-AST-to-model-to-validation seam for document, source, span, entity, and record declarations plus thin document validate/show and recognition show projections. Preserve exact bytes, Unicode-scalar positions, deterministic ordering, stable diagnostics, and no-write/no-locator-I/O behavior. This internal pre-acceptance route is only a dogfood instrument and is not a released or compatibility-stable CLI.
  duration 13p
  status done
  priority 80
  requires:
    IMPLEMENTER 1

task RUN_GRAMMAR_AUTHORING_DOGFOOD STATIC_DUPLICATION_CHECK_ACCEPTED -> GRAMMAR_DOGFOOD_OBSERVED:
  title "Dogfood grammar understanding through the bootstrap read path"
  description |
    Read the normative grammar and EBNF, answer the frozen questions by authoring a bounded .recog document, then run validate and show repeatedly through the actual implementation. Capture reproducible receipts for authoring friction, parser and diagnostic behavior, semantic expressiveness, output usefulness, and responsibility-boundary pressure without treating the operator's interpretation or an LLM response as a golden oracle.
  duration 5p
  status done
  priority 70
  requires:
    IMPLEMENTER 1

task APPLY_GRAMMAR_DOGFOOD_FEEDBACK GRAMMAR_DOGFOOD_OBSERVED -> GRAMMAR_DOGFOOD_REVIEWED:
  title "Disposition grammar dogfood findings before expanding the grammar"
  description |
    Classify every observation as a contract or semantic issue, implementation defect, diagnostic or presentation issue, documentation issue, or out-of-scope reasoning/planning request. Record accepted, rejected, and deferred decisions; update an ADR first for any semantic or public-contract change; revise the remaining point estimates and acceptance evidence before implementation resumes.
  duration 3p
  priority 60
  requires:
    IMPLEMENTER 1
    SEMANTIC_REVIEWER 1

task IMPLEMENT_COMPLETE_PHASE_2_READ_PATH GRAMMAR_DOGFOOD_REVIEWED -> COMPLETE_READ_PATH_ACCEPTED:
  title "Complete the 0.1 ambiguity and constraint read path"
  description |
    Extend the real scanner, recovered AST, typed model, reference resolution, validation, and read-only projections across observation, normalization, variable, candidate, and all five constraint declarations. Validate declaration registries, grounding, candidate membership, and operand shapes without evaluating CSP viability. Make all Phase 1 success and failure fixtures pass with exact stable diagnostics and schema-valid deterministic text/JSON projections.
  duration 21p
  priority 50
  requires:
    IMPLEMENTER 1

task RUN_SPECIFICATION_AUTHORING_DOGFOOD COMPLETE_READ_PATH_ACCEPTED -> SPEC_DOGFOOD_OBSERVED:
  title "Dogfood requirements and architecture understanding"
  description |
    Read requirements, terminology, architecture, and implementation phases; author bounded .recog documents for explicit claims, ambiguity, exclusions, and cross-document references; and exercise validate/show through the actual complete Phase 2 path. Record where supported, allowed, excluded, and unknown are easy to confuse, where the source does not ground a desired constraint, and where requested inference or execution planning belongs outside llmrecog.
  duration 8p
  priority 40
  requires:
    IMPLEMENTER 1

task APPLY_SPECIFICATION_DOGFOOD_FEEDBACK SPEC_DOGFOOD_OBSERVED -> SPEC_DOGFOOD_REVIEWED:
  title "Disposition specification dogfood findings and re-estimate later phases"
  description |
    Review receipts against the frozen questions and corpus digests, separate correctness from usability and missing later-phase behavior, update the accepted/rejected/deferred ledger, and revise Phase 2 acceptance plus the dogfood-first roadmap. Do not broaden the contract merely to encode an ungrounded conclusion or to make the self-produced artifact pass.
  duration 5p
  priority 30
  requires:
    IMPLEMENTER 1
    SEMANTIC_REVIEWER 1

task ACCEPT_PHASE_2_SLICE SPEC_DOGFOOD_REVIEWED -> PHASE_2_ACCEPTED:
  title "Audit and accept the Phase 2 vertical slice"
  description |
    Run focused success and failure checks, npm run check, and git diff --check; verify supported Node targets, schema and fixture parity, deterministic repeated output, core dependency direction, no provider or related-project runtime, no source locator I/O, and no responsibility leakage into CSP inference or execution planning. Review the final diff and record unresolved or deferred work without starting Phase 3, publishing, releasing, tagging, or pushing.
  duration 3p
  priority 20
  requires:
    IMPLEMENTER 1
    SEMANTIC_REVIEWER 1

task INTEGRATE_JSCPD_CHECK BOOTSTRAP_READ_PATH_ACCEPTED -> STATIC_DUPLICATION_CHECK_ACCEPTED:
  title "Integrate the jscpd duplication gate"
  description "Measure the current authored TypeScript and JavaScript baseline, pin jscpd as a development dependency, freeze the minimum clone size, baseline ceiling, and generated-artifact exclusions, connect a deterministic no-report check to npm run check, and review the lockfile, install-script approvals, and npm audit result. Do not refactor semantic code only to reduce a metric or scan normative source fixtures as implementation duplication."
  duration 2p
  status done
  priority 75
  requires:
    IMPLEMENTER 1

